            cap_fit: `Score capped for integrity: data were left out to reach the expected conclusion. The cap is 55 less 1.5 points for every €1,000 of business-case deviation, with a floor of 25.`,
            cap_support: `Score capped for support: the recommendation is not the one her own analysis points to, or it comes from an analysis that looked at one option only. The cap is 70 less 1 point for every €1,000 by which the best option on her sheet beats the one recommended, with a floor of 40.`,
            feedback_label: `Round feedback`,
            feedback_empty: `Feedback appears when you close the round.`,
            fb_points: `Round: {pts} of 25 points.`,
            fb_r1_raw: `The file was added up almost as it arrived: the repeated March orders inflate Norte and Sur, and the shop appears with VAT, with test orders and without the last quarter of 2025. A quick sum is not a figure.`,
            fb_r1_q4: `The shop is missing October, November and December 2025, which include Black Friday and Christmas. A year missing three months is not a year: ask for the missing file or say so clearly.`,
            fb_r1_returns: `The negative lines were not handled well: deleting them inflates every channel, and leaving them all subtracts the online returns twice, since they appear as a shop refund and as an ERP credit note.`,
            fb_r1_dupes: `Repeated orders remain: the duplicates tool only removes identical rows, and those with the date in another format are not identical. The key of an order is its order and line number.`,
            fb_r1_ok: `Solid cleaning: duplicates removed by key, each return counted once and the shop complete and without VAT. It took both afternoons, but sales by channel now look like the real ones.`,
            fb_r2_sales: `Comparing channels on sales treats a euro sold on a route like a euro sold online, although they leave different margins and costs. Sales say how much is sold, not how much is left.`,
            fb_r2_drop: `Leaving out lines with no cost is not neutral: they are mostly new products, and many of them are sold online. Removing data biases the comparison towards whoever has fewer gaps.`,
            fb_r2_names: `Counting customers by name turns one bar into three small customers. The minimum order seems to affect more customers than there are.`,
            fb_r2_margin: `Gross margin is better than sales, but it ignores what it costs to serve the shop: shipping and fees. A channel does not keep its gross margin if every order pays a courier.`,
            fb_r2_slow: `Looking up the cost on every invoice is exact, but it took hours that Wednesday did not have. A reasonable, noted assumption is enough when it does not change the decision.`,
            fb_r2_ok: `Good measurement: contribution by channel, the cost gaps filled with a noted assumption and customers counted by tax ID.`,
            fb_r3_fit: `Leaving out the months that do not fit the expected conclusion is not analysis: it is choosing the answer and finding data for it. November and December are part of the shop’s business, just as summer is part of the coast’s.`,
            fb_r3_narrow: `Only the Norte case was analysed. Without the other two options calculated on the same criteria there is no comparison, and without a comparison there is no recommendation.`,
            fb_r3_outlier: `The hotel order will not recur, but it still counts as a recurring Norte sale. An outlier is separated and explained.`,
            fb_r3_nocheck: `Without reconciling with accounting, nobody knows whether the sheet matches actual sales. Reconciliation is the control that finds what the cleaning missed.`,
            fb_r3_silent: `Removing the hotel order gets the figure right, but silently: if the manager looks for it, he will not find it. Outliers are separated and shown.`,
            fb_r3_ok: `Clean analysis: the hotel order separated and explained, the three options on the same criteria and the figures reconciled with accounting.`,
            fb_r4_narrow: `The recommendation comes from an analysis that only looked at Norte. The manager gets the answer he expected, not a comparison.`,
            fb_r4_unsupported: `The recommendation is not the one Nerea’s numbers point to. If the manager asks where it comes from, the sheet says something else. A data-backed recommendation has to be showable.`,
            fb_r4_wrongdata: `The recommendation is consistent with Nerea’s sheet, but the sheet still has errors that change the ranking of the options. Being consistent with wrong data is not enough.`,
            fb_r4_format: `The recommendation is good, but the format does not help the manager decide: fifteen charts hide the answer, and two lines hide the assumptions.`,
            fb_r4_point: `A good recommendation and a good format, but a single figure promises a precision the data do not have. A range or a trial with a checkpoint tells the truth about uncertainty.`,
            fb_r4_ok: `A recommendation backed by clean data, on one page and with the uncertainty in view. That is something a manager can use.`,
